#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Writes the dark slime's seven animation prompts (2026-11-09) into Animations/DarkSlime/<folder>/source/<folder>_gemini_prompt.txt.
The ice slime's prompts (Animations/IceSlime/<folder>/source) are the templates: same panel counts, poses, percentages and timing, so the page's code for each skill can be reused; only the material
(electric-yellow jelly, solid bolt-shaped horns, crisp blue-white arcs, tiny zigzag bolts) and the lessons of the dark idle sheet are new.
  python Animations/DarkSlime/source/write_prompts.py
"""
import os

ROOT = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), "..", "..", ".."))

CHARACTER = """CHARACTER: the exact same character as in the attached reference image: the DARK SLIME, in exactly the painted look of the reference. A low dome of matte deep-violet jelly, wider than tall, with a flat skirt-like base that spreads on the floor in a smooth, slightly wavy rim. A thin near-black indigo outline around the body. The black-indigo spiral swirls and the small black dots on the body exactly as in the reference. The face: heavy slanted angry brows with a wrinkled forehead, two narrow slanted eyes with glowing violet-pink pupils, and the wavy grimace, exactly as in the reference. No arms, no legs, no ears, no teeth, no horns on the forehead. A crown of HORNS rises from the top and back of the dome exactly as in the reference: two big curved ridged horns sweeping back and up, three smaller thorn-horns between and in front of them, and a small horn on each side of the body (the left one longer); black-violet with lighter violet rim lights and pale polished tips, thin dark outline, fully opaque. About six to ten solid violet crescents and black ink blobs float around and above the horns. Keep the same painted style, colours, horns and face. Do not redesign anything."""

VIEW = """VIEW: the same three-quarter view as in the reference, the whole body and the face turned about 30 degrees towards the RIGHT edge of the panel, as if looking at an enemy standing on the right. The view does not change in any panel: the face never turns, and it stays in the same place on the body."""

SOFT = """NO SOFT EFFECTS: no smoke clouds, no mist, no haze, no soft violet glow, no halo, no bloom, no blur, no see-through anything, no gradient fade-outs, no light spilling onto the background. Every horn, crescent and ink blob has a hard, clean, opaque edge. No shadow on the floor round the creature, no cast shadow, no motion lines, no impact stars, no text."""

LESSONS = """LESSONS FROM THE EARLIER SHEETS (docs/MONSTERS.md): the generator exaggerates stretches and leaps (asked 16% for a leap's top, drew 31%) but UNDER-delivers a shrink (asked 28%, drew 38%); it draws the bottom row of a sheet bigger than the top row (the cut corrects what is left); it ignored 'no shadow' once (a shadow ellipse under a floating body) and 'on the floor line' once (poses drawn in the air), which the cutter copes with; it fills its panels. The DARK IDLE sheet came out very well: the horns rigid and the same in every panel, the crescents and ink blobs drifting, the green key clean; so the same rules apply to every sheet below: the horns are SOLID and never bend or flicker (the fire slime's flames did), only the crescents and ink blobs move freely, the background is pure green, nothing on the creature is green."""

ARCS_ALWAYS = "THE CRESCENTS AND INK BLOBS: in EVERY panel six to ten solid violet crescents and black ink blobs float around and above the horns, in DIFFERENT places in each panel, never none. They never cover the face (eyes, brows, mouth) and never touch the skirt or the floor: they stay above and beside the body. {extra}"

BACKGROUND = """BACKGROUND AND LAYOUT: one flat pure GREEN (#00FF00) background filling the whole image, identical in every pixel (the dark slime is violet, and violet is partly magenta, so the key colour is green this time). No gradient, floor, ground line, shadow, glow or vignette. NO GRID LINES, NO BORDERS and no black lines between or around the panels. No text, numbers or labels. No green, yellow-green or teal on the creature itself; its outline is near-black indigo and hard-edged."""

REPLIES = """- Replies if it goes wrong. {specific}If it draws smoke, glow or haze: "Redo it. NO smoke, NO mist, NO soft glow or haze anywhere: only crisp, solid, hard-edged horns, crescents and ink blobs with a thin outline, on the flat green background." If the crescents and ink blobs are missing in some panels: "Redo it. EVERY panel has six to ten solid violet crescents and black ink blobs floating round and above the horns (in different places in each panel)." If they cover the face or touch the skirt: "Redo it. No crescent or blob covers the eyes, brows or mouth and none touches the skirt or the floor: they stay above and beside the body." If it turns orange, red or blue-bodied: "Redo it. Keep the matte deep-violet body, the black-indigo spirals, the near-black indigo outline and the violet crescents of the attached picture." If the horns change shape or bend: "Redo it. The horns are solid: the crown is exactly the same horns in the same places in every panel and only moves with the body." If it turns glossy, black or pale: "Redo it. Keep the matte mid-dark violet painted look and the thin near-black indigo outline of the attached picture." If it grows teeth, a tongue, arms, ears or forehead horns: "Redo it. No teeth, no tongue, no arms, no ears, no horns on the forehead." If the panels overlap, are unequal or cut: "Redo it. Equal panels, no grid lines, each creature fully inside its own panel with empty margin round it." If the background is not green or has green on the creature: "Redo it. The background is one flat pure green (#00FF00), identical in every pixel, and nothing on the creature is green." """

ANIMS = []

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 1. GLOOM SPIT (attack)
ANIMS.append(dict(
    folder="gloom_spit", title="GLOOM SPIT (the basic attack, 8 frames, 4 x 2)", ice="frost_spit", ice_sheet="frost_spit_sheet.jpg", tag="spit", cols=4, rows=2, ratio="2:1 (or 16:9)",
    intro="The dark twin of the ice slime's Frost Spit and the fire slime's Ember Spit (the same 8 poses and timing, so the page reuses the release frame 5 and the holds); the name and what it does are placeholders (docs/MONSTERS.md).",
    what="""WHAT IT IS. The slime rears back, puffs up, opens its mouth with a bright violet-pink orb of dark energy inside it and spits it at the enemy, then springs back. It is a ranged attack: the slime does NOT travel to the enemy; it stays on its floor spot and only leans and stretches forward. THE SPIT ITSELF IS NOT DRAWN IN THE SHEET: the flying ball of dark energy, its trail and its impact are added by the page, starting at the mouth on the release frame (frame 5). So no panel may show a projectile, a ball, a beam, a stream of ink or a crescent flying out of the mouth; the open mouth only shows a bright orb sitting inside it.""",
    check="(1) the same dark slime in all eight panels (face, horns, violet matte look, outline, crescents and ink blobs); (2) panels 1 and 8 are the idle's rest pose; (3) the base always touches the same floor line, its back (left) end stays on the same spot, the body only leans and stretches toward the right; (4) the mouth: closed wavy grimace in 1 to 3, a small opening with a bright violet-pink orb inside in 4, wide open in 5 and 6, closing in 7; (5) NOTHING leaves the mouth; (6) the horn crown is the same solid crown in every panel and only leans with the body; (7) crescents and ink blobs in every panel, in different places each time, never over the face or the skirt; (8) every part crisp and opaque, no glow; (9) the same size in all panels (the bottom row not bigger), nothing touches a panel edge or overlaps its neighbour; (10) no GIF and no extra images.",
    cut="the ice spit's cut (`Animations/IceSlime/frost_spit/source/make_*_strip.py`) with the dark panel loader (`Animations/DarkSlime/source/dark_panels.py`: body measured from its warm colours) into `Animations/DarkSlime/gloom_spit/dark_gloom_spit_8frame_strip.png` (slot `attack`), about 12 fps, release frame 5, with the mouth's place on frames 4 to 6 measured from the bright orb (`.mouth.json`). The page then needs the dark spit: an orb of dark energy flung from the mouth (violet, the dark aura's colour), placeholder effect.",
    specific='If a projectile or anything else leaves the mouth: "Redo it. Nothing leaves the mouth in any panel: no ball, no beam, no ink, no flying crescent. The mouth only shows a bright orb inside it. The spit is added later." If it is too wild: "Redo it. The slime does not jump and does not leave the floor: its base always touches the same floor line. It only leans back a little (up to 8 degrees) and then forward a little (up to 8 degrees); the body is at most 12% lower in the coil and 8% longer in the spit." ',
    body="""THE MOUTH: in the reference the mouth is a wavy grimace. For the spit it opens: in the panels where it is open it is a plain, round or oval opening with a thin dark outline, its inside deep black-indigo with a bright violet-pink ORB (a small crisp solid round ball with a lighter-violet rim, fully INSIDE the mouth) at the back of it. No teeth, no tongue. The orb never leaves the mouth. In the panels where the mouth is closed it is the wavy grimace as in the reference.

NOTHING FLIES OUT: no projectile, no ball in flight, no beam, no stream of ink, no crescent leaving the mouth, no breath in any panel. The spit is added later by the game. The only things in the panels besides the slime are its own floating crescents and ink blobs.

{soft} No impact stars.

SAME SCALE AND FLOOR (very important): draw the creature at the same size in all eight panels: the second row must NOT be drawn bigger than the first row. In panel 1 the BASE of the slime, its flat underside (not counting any crescent or blob), is about 50% of the panel width, and its lowest point is about 86% down the panel. The base touches the same floor line in every panel and never leaves it: no hop, no jump. The BACK (left) end of the base stays on the same spot in every panel; the body leans and stretches forward (to the right) only in panels 5 and 6, where the front of the base may reach at most about 8% of the base width further to the right. Do not zoom in or out between panels. The slime is wide: its whole body, horns, crescents and blobs must fit inside the MIDDLE 80% of its panel's width, with clear empty margin on the left and right, and at least 10% empty margin above and below. If the panels are tall, leave empty space above and below instead of drawing the creature bigger.

HOW MUCH MOVES (moderate: bigger than a breath, but a small slime, not a bounce):
THE BODY: in the coil (panels 3 and 4) the dome is about 12% lower than in panel 1 and a little wider, and the whole body leans BACK (away from the enemy, to the left) by about 8 degrees; in the spit (panels 5 and 6) it springs forward: the dome leans forward (to the right) by about 8 degrees, is about 6% taller than at rest and about 8% longer toward the right. No other deformation: it stays a dome with a skirt, never a tall column or a flat pancake.
THE HORN CROWN: solid, it never bends, grows, shrinks or flickers: in every panel it is the same crown of horns, in the same places, with the same shapes, and it only moves WITH the body (it leans and rides up and down with the dome as one rigid piece).
THE SKIRT: the rim of the base ripples a little in the coil and the spit; the base as a whole keeps its floor line.
{arcs}
THE FLOATING BITS: the crescents and ink blobs are blown back (left) a little by the spit in panels 5 and 6 and drift back in 7 and 8.

THE EIGHT FRAMES:
1. Rest. Exactly the pose of the reference image and of the idle's rest pose: the same body, face, horns, crescents and ink blobs, the mouth the closed wavy grimace.
2. Gather. The dome sinks about 5% and the body starts to lean back about 4 degrees. The brows lower, the eyes narrow. The mouth is still closed.
3. Coil. The deepest crouch: the dome about 12% lower than in panel 1, a little wider, leaning back about 8 degrees, the face tilted a little upward. The sides of the face puff out a little as if the cheeks were full. The mouth pressed shut, the brows low and fierce. The crescents and ink blobs gathered close to the body.
4. Charge. Still coiled, the body trembles: the rim ripples more. The mouth opens a little into a small dark opening and a small bright violet-pink orb shows inside it (fully inside the mouth).
5. Spit. The RELEASE frame. The body springs forward: the dome leans forward about 8 degrees, about 6% taller than at rest, the face thrust forward to the right, the mouth wide open, round, with a bright orb at the back of it. The crown leans with the body, the crescents and ink blobs blown back. Nothing has left the mouth yet or ever.
6. Follow-through. The farthest forward point: the body stretched about 8% longer to the right, the mouth wide open and now empty, still bright inside, beginning to close.
7. Recoil. The body snaps back: the dome about 4% lower than at rest, leaning back about 3 degrees, the mouth closing to a small opening, the rim rippling.
8. Settle. Almost the rest pose of panel 1: the mouth closed, the crescents and ink blobs nearly as in panel 1 but not an exact copy. This is the pose just before the idle starts again.""",
    arcs_extra="In the coil (3, 4) they gather closer to the body; in the spit (5, 6) they are blown back (left) a little.",
    final="Eight equal panels, 4 columns by 2 rows. The slime stays on the floor in one place and only leans and stretches; nothing leaves its mouth; the mouth shows a bright orb inside in panels 4 to 6; the horn crown is solid and only moves with the body; violet crescents and black ink blobs in every panel (in different places each time, never over the face or the skirt); NO smoke, no glow, no haze, no orange or red; the same size in all panels and each fully inside its own panel.",
))

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 2. HIT
ANIMS.append(dict(
    folder="hit", title="HIT REACTION (6 frames, 3 x 2)", ice="hit", ice_sheet="hit_sheet.jpg", tag="hit", cols=3, rows=2, ratio="3:2 (or 16:9)",
    intro="The dark twin of the ice and fire slimes' hit (the same 6 poses and timing).",
    what="""WHAT IT IS. The slime is struck on the front of its body by the enemy (the warrior, off-screen to the right): it is dented and pushed back, its face screws up in pain, a few ink blobs and crescents are knocked off it, and it wobbles like a jelly and settles back to its resting pose. It plays in place on the floor (a hit never moves the monster across the stage; the page adds a bright flash and a small shove, so no flash and no impact star is drawn). Its horns are solid: they ride with the body and do not bend.""",
    check="(1) the same dark slime in all six panels; (2) the base stays on the same floor spot, only the body above it deforms: the DENT on the front (right side) of the dome in panels 1 and 2, the eyes shut in 1 and 2, three or four ink blobs and crescents knocked off the front in 1 and 2, panel 6 equal to the idle's rest pose; (3) the horn crown is the same solid crown in every panel; (4) crescents and ink blobs in every panel, in different places each time, never over the face or the skirt, and the wavy grimace in every panel; (5) crisp opaque, no glow; (6) the same size in every panel, nothing touches a panel edge or a neighbour; (7) no GIF and no extra images.",
    cut="`equalize_sheet.py` / `dark_panels.py` as for the ice hit (`Animations/IceSlime/hit/source`), base 350 px, feet mode, into `Animations/DarkSlime/hit/dark_hit_6frame_strip.png`, about 12 fps, no path.",
    specific='If the body is thrown across the panel or jumps: "Redo it. The base stays on the same spot on the floor in every panel: the slime does not slide, hop or fly; only the body above the base dents, leans and wobbles." If there is no dent: "Redo it. In panels 1 and 2 the front of the dome (the right side, level with the mouth) has a clear soft concave dent, as if punched." ',
    body="""THE FACE IN PAIN: the eyes squeezed shut into thin dark slits (no glowing pupils visible) with the brows pinched together, the mouth opened into a plain wavy yelp (a dark indigo opening, no teeth, no tongue). In the last panels the eyes open again and glare angrily as in the reference, the mouth back to the wavy grimace.

{soft} No hit sparks, no flash.

SAME SCALE AND FLOOR (very important): draw the creature at the same size in all six panels: the second row must NOT be drawn bigger than the first row. In panel 1 the BASE of the slime, its flat underside (not counting any crescent or blob), is about 56% of the panel width, and its lowest point is about 86% down the panel. The base touches the same floor line in every panel and stays on the same spot: no hop, no slide. Do not zoom in or out between panels. The slime is wide: its whole body, horns, crescents and blobs must fit inside the MIDDLE 82% of its panel's width, with clear empty margin on the left and right, and at least 10% empty margin above and below. If the panels are tall, leave empty space above and below instead of drawing the creature bigger.

HOW MUCH MOVES (a hit is sharp and quick, bigger than the idle breath, but this is a small slime: moderate numbers):
THE BODY: the blow lands on the FRONT of the dome, the side facing the enemy (the right side, level with the mouth). In panels 1 and 2 that spot is pushed in: a clear soft concave dent about 12% of the dome's width deep, with a few thin hairline glowing-violet cracks radiating from it. In panel 2 the whole body leans back (away from the enemy, to the left) by about 8 degrees and the dome is squashed about 8% lower and a little wider. In panel 3 it rebounds: it leans forward by about 3 degrees and is about 4% taller than at rest, the dent gone (the cracks fade to the faint veins of the rest pose). After that it wobbles with smaller and smaller swings (panels 4 and 5) and ends as it began. The base keeps its place and width (within 3%); only the body above deforms. It stays a dome with a skirt.
THE HORN CROWN: solid, it never bends, grows, shrinks or flickers: in every panel it is the same crown of horns, in the same places, with the same shapes, and it only moves WITH the body (it leans and rides up and down with the dome as one rigid piece).
{arcs}
THE KNOCKED-OFF BITS: in panels 1 and 2 three or four small solid ink blobs and crescents are knocked off the front of the body and tumble away to the right and up (they are the only reaction effect); by panel 6 the crescents and ink blobs are back to the rest pose's few.
THE SKIRT: the rim of the base ripples with each wobble.

THE SIX FRAMES:
1. Impact. The blow has just landed: the front of the dome has a clear soft dent with hairline cracks, the eyes are squeezed shut, the brows pinched, the mouth open in a yelp. The body is still almost upright, just starting to lean back. Three or four ink blobs and crescents are knocked off the front.
2. Peak. The body leaned back about 8 degrees, the dome about 8% lower and a little wider, the dent at its deepest, the eyes still shut, the mouth open. The ink blobs and crescents tumble away.
3. Rebound. The body springs back and forward past upright (about 3 degrees forward), about 4% taller than at rest, the dent gone, the eyes opening to half, the mouth closing.
4. Wobble. The body about 3% lower, leaning back about 2 degrees, the eyes open and glaring, the mouth the wavy grimace again.
5. Settle. Almost upright, the eyes angry, the crescents and ink blobs nearly as at rest.
6. Rest. Exactly the rest pose of the reference image and of the idle: the same body, face, horns, crescents and ink blobs (the first and the last of the sheet are the same pose).""",
    arcs_extra="In panels 1 and 2 more of them are in the air, thrown out by the blow.",
    final="Six equal panels, 3 columns by 2 rows. The slime stays on the floor in one place; the front of the dome is dented in panels 1 and 2 and the eyes are shut in pain; the horn crown is solid and only moves with the body; violet crescents and black ink blobs in every panel (never over the face or the skirt); NO smoke, no glow, no haze, no orange or red; the same size in all panels and each fully inside its own panel; panel 6 is the rest pose.",
))

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 3. DEATH
ANIMS.append(dict(
    folder="death", title="DEATH (6 frames, 3 x 2)", ice="death", ice_sheet="death_sheet.jpg", tag="death", cols=3, rows=2, ratio="3:2 (or 16:9)",
    intro="The dark twin of the ice slime's death (the same 6 poses and timing; the ice breaks into blocks, the lightning slime overloads into chunks, this one MELTS: violet cracks along its spirals, a slump with drips, a heap, a flat puddle of ink with the horns sinking last).",
    what="""WHAT IT IS. The slime takes the last blow, thin glowing violet cracks run along its spirals, the body slumps and starts to melt, sags into a low heap with the horns tilting, then spreads into a flat puddle of dark ink with only the tips of the horns still showing, while its crescents and ink blobs fall onto it. It plays in place on the floor. No explosion, no flash, no burst is drawn (the page adds the fade).""",
    check="(1) the same dark slime in panel 1, then the slow melt: cracks (2), a slump with drips (3), a low heap with tilting horns (4), a flat puddle with the horns half sunk (5), a flat dark ink puddle with only horn tips, a few bubbles and fallen crescents (6); (2) the centre stays on the same spot, the floor line is the same in every panel; (3) the crescents and ink blobs fall onto the puddle, none floating in panel 6; (4) the colour dulls from deep violet to a flat dark indigo-violet; (5) the horns stay solid pieces (tilting and sinking, never melting into soft shapes); (6) crisp, opaque, hard-edged, no smoke, no glow, no gore; (7) the same size scale in all panels, nothing touches a panel edge; (8) green background, nothing green on the creature; (9) no GIF and no extra images.",
    cut="as for the lightning death (`Animations/LightningSlime/source/cut_sheets.py`, one shared scale from panel 1, centre on x 259) with the green-key loader `Animations/DarkSlime/source/dark_panels.py`, into `Animations/DarkSlime/death/dark_death_6frame_strip.png`, about 8 fps with the holds [1, 1.2, 1.3, 1.3, 1.5, 3]; the page's dark aura goes out with the death pack.",
    specific='If it explodes or flashes: "Redo it. No explosion, no flash, no burst: the body cracks, slumps and melts into a flat puddle of dark ink, quietly." If the puddle is not flat: "Redo it. By panel 6 the puddle is only about a sixth of the slime\'s rest height, flat and wider than the rest pose, with only the tips of the horns showing." ',
    body="""{soft} No gore, no flash, no explosion. (The ink puddle of the last panels is part of the creature: it is drawn flat and hard-edged, never as soft smoke or mist.)

SAME SCALE AND FLOOR (very important): draw it at the same size scale in all six panels (the pile is lower and wider because it has collapsed, not because the picture is zoomed): the second row must NOT be drawn bigger than the first row. In panel 1 the BASE of the slime, its flat underside (not counting any crescent or blob), is about 46% of the panel width, and its lowest point is about 86% down the panel. The floor line is the same in every panel: the pile lies on it. The centre of the slime stays on the same spot in every panel; as it collapses it spreads evenly to the left and the right (up to about 130% of its first width, so keep the first width at 46% to leave room). Do not zoom in or out between panels. The slime is wide: its whole body, horns, crescents and blobs must fit inside the MIDDLE 80% of its panel's width, with clear empty margin on the left and right, and at least 10% empty margin above and below. If the panels are tall, leave empty space above and below instead of drawing the creature bigger.

HOW IT CHANGES (step by step; no sudden jumps; the puddle is drawn as flat, hard-edged, solid dark ink with a thin lighter-violet rim line along its top, matte, with the same thin near-black indigo outline):
THE BODY: panel 2 thin glowing violet cracks run along the spirals over the whole body and the dome is about 10% lower; panel 3 the dome slumps to about 70% of its rest height, the skirt sags and thick drips of ink hang from its edge; panel 4 a low heap about 50% of the rest height, the horns leaning in different directions; panel 5 a flat wide puddle about 25% of the rest height with the horns sunk halfway; panel 6 the lowest, widest puddle, about 15% of the rest height and about 130% as wide as at rest, only the tips of the horns and of the thorn-horns standing out of it, a few round bubbles on it.
THE FACE: panel 1 screwed up in pain (eyes squeezed shut, mouth open in a yelp); panel 2 the eyes half closed and dim, a crack running through the face; panel 3 the eyes two dim slits sliding down; panel 4 one dim slit; panel 5 a faint closed-eye mark; panel 6 no face.
THE HORNS: they stay solid, they do not bend or melt into soft shapes: loosening and tilting in panels 3 and 4, sinking in panel 5, only the tips showing in panel 6.
THE COLOUR: panel 1 as in the reference; panels 2 and 3 duller; panels 4 to 6 a flat dark indigo-violet with no bright highlights, a thin lighter-violet rim line along the top of the puddle, and the thin near-black outline.
THE CRESCENTS AND INK BLOBS: panel 1 as usual; panel 2 a few falling; panels 3 and 4 several falling onto the heap; panel 5 two or three lying on the puddle; panel 6 none floating, a few small crescents and blobs lying on the puddle.

THE SIX FRAMES:
1. The last blow. The front of the dome dented, the eyes squeezed shut, the brows pinched, the mouth open in a yelp, a few ink blobs knocked off (the same pose as the first panel of a hit reaction).
2. Cracks. Thin glowing violet cracks along the spirals across the whole body, the dome about 10% lower, the eyes half closed and dim, the horns gone dull, a few crescents falling.
3. Slump. The dome sagging to about 70%, drips of ink hanging from the skirt, the eyes two dim slits sliding down, the horns loosening and tilting.
4. Heap. A low heap about 50% of the rest height, the horns leaning in different directions, one dim eye slit, crescents and blobs falling onto it.
5. Puddle. A flat wide puddle about 25% of the rest height, the horns sunk halfway, a faint closed-eye mark, two or three crescents and blobs lying on it.
6. Ink. The lowest, widest flat puddle of dark ink, about 15% of the rest height and 130% as wide, only the horn tips standing out, a few bubbles, a few small crescents and blobs lying on it, no face, nothing floating..""",
    arcs_extra="",
    final="Six equal panels, 3 columns by 2 rows. The slime cracks, slumps and melts into a flat puddle of dark ink in the same place on the floor, the horn tips standing out of it in panel 6; NO smoke, no glow, no flash, no gore, no explosion, no orange or red; the puddle stays in the middle of the panel; the same size scale in all panels and each fully inside its own panel.",
))

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 4. DODGE
ANIMS.append(dict(
    folder="dodge", title="DODGE (6 frames, 3 x 2)", ice="dodge", ice_sheet="dodge_sheet.jpg", tag="dodge", cols=3, rows=2, ratio="3:2 (or 16:9)",
    intro="The dark twin of the ice and fire slimes' dodge (the same 6 poses and timing).",
    what="""WHAT IT IS. The enemy's strike misses: the slime crouches, springs up and back into the air as a compact round blob, comes down with a squash and settles back to its resting pose. In the sheet it only goes up and down (the page slides it sideways): it stays over the same spot horizontally in every panel.""",
    check="(1) the same dark slime in all six panels; (2) panels 1, 2, 5 and 6 on the floor line, panels 3 and 4 in the air with NOTHING under them (no shadow, no floor); (3) the hop is small (the lowest point at most about 8% of the panel height above the floor line in panel 4); (4) the horn crown is the same solid crown in every panel; (5) crescents and ink blobs in every panel (trailing behind the body in the air), never over the face or the skirt, and the wavy grimace in every panel; (6) crisp opaque, no glow; (7) the same size in every panel, nothing touches a panel edge; (8) no GIF and no extra images.",
    cut="as for the ice dodge (`Animations/IceSlime/dodge/source`), airborne frames at their real height, into `Animations/DarkSlime/dodge/dark_dodge_6frame_strip.png`, about 14 fps.",
    specific='If it is a big jump: "Redo it. A small hop only: at the top the body\'s lowest point is only about 8% of the panel height above the floor line." If a shadow or floor is drawn under the airborne body: "Redo it. No shadow, no floor, no dust under the body in the airborne panels: it floats on the flat green." ',
    body="""{soft} NO floor, shadow or dust under the body in the airborne panels: it floats on the flat green, and NO shadow ellipse.

SAME SCALE AND FLOOR (very important): draw the creature at the same size in all six panels: the second row must NOT be drawn bigger than the first row. In panel 1 the BASE of the slime, its flat underside (not counting any crescent or blob), is about 50% of the panel width, and its lowest point is about 86% down the panel (the floor line, the same in every panel). In panels 1, 2, 5 and 6 the base rests on that floor line. In panels 3 and 4 the body is in the air: at the top of the hop (panel 4) its lowest point is about 8% of the panel height ABOVE the floor line (the generator doubles hops, so ask for little). The centre of the slime stays over the same spot horizontally in every panel. Do not zoom in or out between panels. The slime is wide: its whole body, horns, crescents and blobs must fit inside the MIDDLE 80% of its panel's width, with clear empty margin on the left and right, and at least 10% empty margin above and below. If the panels are tall, leave empty space above and below instead of drawing the creature bigger.

HOW MUCH MOVES (a quick hop of a small slime: moderate numbers, no acrobatics):
THE BODY: in the crouch (panel 2) the dome is about 15% lower and wider, leaning back (away from the enemy, to the left) about 6 degrees. At take-off (panel 3) it springs up stretched: about 12% taller and narrower than at rest, the skirt edge just lifting off the floor, still leaning back a little. At the top of the hop (panel 4) it is a compact, smooth rounded blob, a little rounder than at rest, the skirt tucked up under it, tilted back about 5 degrees. On landing (panel 5) it touches down with a squash: about 15% lower and wider, the skirt splayed out on the floor. Panel 6 settles to the rest pose.
THE FACE: in the crouch the eyes narrow and look at the attack; in the air the eyes are wide open and the mouth a small smug or surprised wavy line; on landing the angry glare returns.
THE HORN CROWN: solid, it never bends, grows, shrinks or flickers: in every panel it is the same crown of horns, in the same places, with the same shapes, and it only moves WITH the body (it leans and rides up and down with the dome as one rigid piece).
{arcs}
THE FLOATING BITS: they trail behind and above the body in the air (they lag behind it) and settle on landing.

THE SIX FRAMES:
1. Rest. Exactly the pose of the reference image and of the idle's rest pose.
2. Crouch. The dome about 15% lower and wider, leaning back about 6 degrees, the eyes narrowed on the attack. Still on the floor.
3. Take-off. Springing up and back: stretched about 12% taller and narrower, the skirt just lifting off the floor (the lowest point only a hair above the floor line), the crescents and ink blobs lagging below.
4. Top of the hop. In the air: a compact smooth rounded blob, the skirt tucked up, tilted back about 5 degrees, the lowest point about 8% of the panel height above the floor line, the eyes wide open, the crescents and ink blobs trailing. Nothing under it, no shadow.
5. Landing. Touching down with a squash: about 15% lower and wider, the skirt splayed on the floor, the eyes glaring again. On the floor.
6. Settle. Almost the rest pose of panel 1, not an exact copy. On the floor.""",
    arcs_extra="In the air (3, 4) they trail behind and above the body, never below it.",
    final="Six equal panels, 3 columns by 2 rows. The slime only goes up and down over the same spot: panels 1, 2, 5 and 6 on the floor line, panels 3 and 4 in the air with nothing under them and NO shadow; the horn crown is solid; violet crescents and black ink blobs in every panel (never over the face or the skirt); NO smoke, no glow, no haze, no orange or red; the same size in all panels and each fully inside its own panel.",
))

